laurel 2770: rear flashlight (torch) on the Mi A3. PMI632 flash LED module (qcom,qpnp-flash-led-v2, SPMI SID 3 0xD300, pmi632.dtsi:519; laurel uses torch_0 = LED1 only, ires 12.5 mA, DT max 950 mA) through the one SPMI core (user SWEET_SPMI_TORCH, sweet_spmi.c 2710 rule). Sequence as leds-qpnp-flash-v2.c qpnp_flash_led_switch_set: IRES 0x47, STROBE_CTRL 0x49 bit 2 = 0 (SW), TGR_CURRENT 0x43, SAFETY_TMR 0x40 = 0x13 (off: torch), MOD_CTRL 0x46 bit 7, then the PMI632 charger flash boost VREG_OK (SID 2 0xA607 bit 4, 5 ms x 60; 0xA608 & 7 = 7 = error), then EN_LED_CTRL 0x4C bit 0; off = EN_LED 0, MOD_CTRL off, TGR 0, timer 0x13. Every write read back; a failure = off for the boot (the off sequence still runs). Policy: 1..100 % = 12.5..150 mA (cap 150 mA, static assert <= DT max), auto-off 600 s, no light at an OTST level (LED_STATUS2 0x09 bits 0-2), lit: an OTST level, the led-fault bit (INT_RT bit 0; STATUS1 short/open and VPH droop named in the line) or a charger flash error turn it off (watch 100 ms); 3 faults = off. Halt/restart/panic: laurel_torch_quiesce (emergency SPMI writes, SweetPlatformExpert). iOS: /dev/laureltorch root:mobile 0660 (write "0".."100", read the state), LaurelTorch IOService (IOResources match) starts it; after the root mount IODeviceTree:/product/camera "flash" (MobileGestalt camera-flash = the Control Center button) only when the root has LaurelFlashlight.driver (userland/laurel/flashlight: mediaserverd plug-in that gives FigFlashlight a device whose TorchLevel lands here and starts the FigFlashlight server). Lines: `LAUREL TORCH: on: PMI632 flash LED SID3 0xd300 (...)` or `LAUREL TORCH: off: <why>`, `LAUREL TORCH UI: on|off: <why>`, `LAUREL TORCH: lit: P % = M mA (code C) by PROC`, `LAUREL TORCH: dark: <why> (lit N ms)`. Kill switch torch=0. Details: docs/laurel_sprout/torch.md.

